name: proxy-material-grace-dir-mtime-bug
description: "Diagnosed 2026-08-12 — proxy-material reaper grace window stats only the dir mtime, so re-staged material for old sandboxes isn't protected and gets pruned mid-recreate, failing ContainerCreate with \"bind source path does not exist\""
metadata: 
  node_type: memory
  type: project
  originSessionId: d41c6f69-123c-4e79-b9a7-5569d7717a2c
  modified: 2026-08-13T04:58:51.404Z
---

Diagnosed 2026-08-12 (sbx_febbbyq0knzng6yq error state): during a spec-change
container replace, the sandbox briefly has no container. The proxy-material
reaper (`reconcileSandboxMaterial` / `proxyagent.OrphanedSandboxIDs`) should
protect in-flight creates with a 15-min grace window, but `materialModTime`
(pool-agent/proxyagent/proxyagent.go) stats only the material **directory** —
while `EnsureSandboxMaterial` overwrites existing files in place, which does
not bump the dir mtime. So re-staged material for an hours-old sandbox looks
stale and is pruned between EnsureSandboxMaterial and ContainerCreate →
Docker fails with `invalid mount config for type "bind": bind source path
does not exist`. The doc comment on OrphanedSandboxIDs says "youngest on-disk
file", so the implementation contradicts its own contract. Made worse by
pool-agent container replacement churn: old + new agents both run reapers
against the shared host tree. Server side records it as a settled failure
(ADR 0017 §4) — errorMessage latched, no retry until new intent; user
recovery is `disco box sandbox repair` (ADR 0035, added 2026-08-12: one
intent that tears down via provider Archive, rebuilds, then starts).
The reaper grace bug itself is NOT yet fixed as of 2026-08-12.
func OrphanedSandboxIDs(root layout.Root, projectID, poolID string, liveSandboxIDs []string, minAge time.Duration) ([]string, error) {
	live := make(map[string]struct{}, len(liveSandboxIDs))
	for _, id := range liveSandboxIDs {
		live[id] = struct{}{}
	}

	var errs []error
	candidates := map[string]struct{}{}
	// Only this project's pool-scoped material root is scanned. Client certs
	// (CertDir/clients) and sentinel registrations live in per-host shared
	// locations keyed by sandbox ID; scanning those would surface other pools'
	// and other projects' sandboxes as candidates on a shared daemon. Every sandbox always has a
	// material dir here, so it is a complete record of this pool's sandboxes;
	// the shared cert/sentinel entries are reclaimed by ID when their material
	// orphan is pruned.
	base := PoolSandboxMaterialRoot(root, projectID, poolID)
	entries, err := os.ReadDir(base)
	if err != nil {
		if !os.IsNotExist(err) {
			errs = append(errs, fmt.Errorf("scan %s: %w", base, err))
		}
	}
	for _, entry := range entries {
		if entry.IsDir() {
			candidates[entry.Name()] = struct{}{}
		}
	}

	cutoff := time.Now().Add(-minAge)
	var orphans []string
	for id := range candidates {
		if _, ok := live[id]; ok {
			continue
		}
		// Ignore names that could not have been produced by EnsureSandboxMaterial
		// rather than risk removing something unexpected.
		if validateIDSegment("sandbox", id) != nil {
			continue
		}
		// Protect material that is still being staged for an in-flight
		// CreateSandbox. Only staged directories carry a grace window; a
		// sentinel-only leftover (its material already gone) is always eligible.
		if minAge > 0 {
			if modTime, hasDir := materialModTime(root, projectID, poolID, id); hasDir && modTime.After(cutoff) {
				continue
			}
		}
		orphans = append(orphans, id)
	}
	sort.Strings(orphans)
	return orphans, errors.Join(errs...)
}
